WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:04.717
You checked nine Kerberos
accounts in a fictional domain,

3
00:00:04.717 --> 00:00:07.999
read a plan with five writes,
each with its request,

4
00:00:07.999 --> 00:00:13.361
change record and the identity that sends
it, an island list and a reconciliation,

5
00:00:13.361 --> 00:00:15.763
applied the plan to a fake by its hash,

6
00:00:15.763 --> 00:00:20.325
as the pipeline and as a person, and
saw a plan nobody approved refused.

7
00:00:20.325 --> 00:00:25.910
The evidence an ISSO keeps for Gate 5 from
this module is the plan with its approved

8
00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:29.606
hash, the findings, the island
list, the reconciliation,

9
00:00:29.606 --> 00:00:34.862
and the two apply folders' results and
manifests, all dated, and the test result.

10
00:00:34.862 --> 00:00:37.937
Before you ship, work through
the chapter's checklist.

11
00:00:37.937 --> 00:00:42.213
Next is Module 9: govern
AI agent identities.

12
00:00:42.213 --> 00:00:47.659
Agents follow every gate you've done so far,
and add three things: an agent can act,

13
00:00:47.659 --> 00:00:52.750
a blueprint holds every agent's
credentials, and creation has to be gated.
